This function reads a configuration file from `configPath` if it exists and returns the parsed JSON object.

- It first checks whether the file exists using `fs.existsSync(configPath)`.
- If the file exists, it tries to read and parse it with `JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(configPath))`.
- If parsing or reading fails, it logs an error and returns an empty object `{}`.
- If the file does not exist, it also returns an empty object `{}`.

One important detail: `fs.readFileSync(configPath)` returns a `Buffer` unless an encoding is provided. In many cases, `JSON.parse` expects a string, so it's safer to read the file as UTF-8 text.

```javascript
function readConfig() {
    if (fs.existsSync(configPath)) {
        try {
            return JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(configPath, 'utf8'));
        } catch (error) {
            console.error('Error reading config:', error);
            return {};
        }
    }
    return {};
}
```
